Comment: Debian policy 12.5 requires this document, and Tauri's deb bundler does
 not write one, so it is installed through `bundle.linux.deb.files` in
 src-tauri/tauri.conf.json. Third-party attribution for the Rust and npm
 dependencies compiled into the executable is installed separately at
 /usr/lib/FontCarver/licenses/, where THIRD_PARTY.md records the project's
 attributions and license rulings and DEPENDENCIES.json indexes every retained
 upstream notice with its SHA-256. This document covers FontCarver's own source
 only; the shared libraries this package depends on carry their own copyright
 documents from their own packages.

