Comment: The executable statically links its Rust dependency graph and embeds
 the built frontend, so it carries the copyright and licenses of those packages
 as well as FontCarver's own. They are not restated here: the full inventory
 ships with the package, under /usr/lib/FontCarver/licenses/. THIRD_PARTY.md
 there records the project's attributions and exact-version license rulings,
 DEPENDENCIES.json lists every package with its version, declared license
 expression, upstream source archive and the SHA-256 of each retained notice,
 and the notice texts themselves sit beside it under dependencies/. Every one of
 those licenses is permissive.

